Measured on PR1100 (01ac7706): after browser forward World stayed at 0 instead of ~2750 px because
its content arrives later than the browser's restore window; back is restored natively.
scrollRestore2029 leaves the browser in charge and adds: (1) POP with a remembered offset: once the
document is tall enough, scroll DOWN to it if the page is >40px above (bounded 4s, cancelled by
touch/wheel/key/pointer, instant jump); (2) PUSH to another pathname without a hash starts at the top;
(3) every location with a hash is left to the page that owns the anchor. Remembers offsets per history
key (session storage, bounded) and ignores the clamp caused by the page being swapped out.

